# Astro site

Astro 7 static site (`output: "static"`) with cascivo on React islands, deployed as Cloudflare
static assets (`wrangler.jsonc`, `./dist`). `integrations: [react(), cascivo()]`: `@astrojs/react`
renders islands, `@cascivo/astro` injects the CSS layer order, the theme and the no-flash script.

- UI: cascivo first. `@cascivo/react` and `--cascivo-*` tokens before own markup or CSS; no
  Tailwind, CSS-in-JS or other component library. Look components up in https://cascivo.com/llms.txt.
- Compose cascivo in a `.tsx` component and hydrate that (`<Hello client:visible />`); never hydrate
  a `@cascivo/react` export directly from `.astro`. No Preact islands: server-rendered Preact
  islands fail under Astro (cascivo `docs/USING-WITH-ASTRO.md`).
- Astro runs through package scripts (`astro dev`, `astro build`); never `vp run`.
- Astro's own `vite` resolves to the Vite+ core through the root override: one vite in the lockfile.
- oxlint does not lint `.astro` templates; only TS/TSX is linted. Review `.astro` files by hand.
  oxfmt `.astro` support is experimental and off, so `format:check` excludes `.astro` files.
- `typecheck` is `tsc --noEmit` (TS/TSX only); `astro check` needs the TypeScript JS API.
- Tests: `vp test run`; component tests opt in to happy-dom with `// @vitest-environment happy-dom`.
- Previews deploy to `<app>-preview` as alias `pr-<n>`. Never create `<app>-preview` by hand.
- Secrets set on the -preview Worker are readable by every PR.
- `kv`/`d1`/`r2`/`queue`/`service` ids in `env.preview` must be preview-only resources; previews share that data.
